# Secrets — never commit (Phase-0 capture creds, local env)
.phase0.env
.env
*.local

# Build output — anchor to repo root so these ignore ONLY the compiled binaries,
# not the cmd/loomarr and cmd/loomarr-ingest source directories (a bare pattern
# matches at any depth).
/bin/
/dist/
/loomarr
/loomarr-ingest

# SQLite dev databases
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Runtime data directories. ⚠ THE GLOB IS THE POINT — this was `/data/` alone, and a run
# pointed at a NON-default directory walked straight past it: 170 image files (27.6 MB
# packed, ~21% of the repo) were committed under `data-p5/` in dfeaee36 before anyone
# noticed. `/data/` was not wrong, it was just an exact name, and the data dir is
# configurable — so the one directory it covered was the only one it could ever cover.
# `/data*/` covers data-p5, data-p6 and whatever the next ad-hoc run is called, without
# anyone maintaining a list. Verified safe: `data-p5` is the only tracked path matching
# `^data`, so this hides nothing real.
/data*/

# Go
*.test
*.out
# ⚠ NOT `coverage.*` — that pattern also swallows SOURCE files. `internal/filler/coverage.go`
# (V29a) was written, tested green locally, and committed as a test file with no implementation
# behind it, because `git add -A` silently skipped it and `git status` reported a clean tree. The
# profile artifact is already covered by `*.out` above; name the rest explicitly.
coverage.html
coverage.txt

# Node / FE (web/ added in Phase 13)
node_modules/
web/apps/web/dist/

# The embedded SPA build output — `make fe` fills this; only .gitkeep is tracked
# so `//go:embed all:dist` compiles on a Go-only checkout (internal/web/embed.go).
/internal/web/dist/*
!/internal/web/dist/.gitkeep

# Air (dev live-reload) build output — the compiled dev binary, never committed.
/tmp/
/build-errors.log

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.playwright-mcp/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# ⚠ `.claude/settings.json` is TRACKED (it used to be ignored, here, on this line). It
# carries the WorktreeCreate/WorktreeRemove/SessionStart hook wiring, and a gitignored
# settings file cannot deliver hooks to anyone — not another machine, not a fresh clone,
# not a new worktree. That is the one thing the hooks exist to fix, so ignoring the file
# that configures them defeated the purpose. Personal, machine-specific overrides belong
# in `.claude/settings.local.json`, which stays ignored below.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code's DEFAULT worktree location, which this repo does not use — the hooks place
# worktrees as siblings (`../loomarr-<name>`) instead, because `make e2e` bind-mounts the
# repo ROOT (`-v "$(PWD):/work"`) and would otherwise mount every worktree's ~450MB of
# node_modules into the Playwright container. Ignored anyway as insurance: if the hooks are
# ever absent or fail, the native default takes over and a stray worktree must not be
# committable into the main checkout.
.claude/worktrees/
.filler-drop/
.cmp-review/
scratch-*.png
.filler-smoke/
